.TH scan_human 3
.SH NAME
scan_human \- parse a number with human-readable suffixes
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <lib/scan.h>

size_t \fBscan_human\fR(const char *\fIsrc\fR, uint64 *\fIdest\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscan_human\fR parses a number from \fIsrc\fR, which may be followed by
a multiplier suffix. The suffixes 'k' or 'K' multiply the value by 1024,
'M' multiplies by 1024^2, and 'G' multiplies by 1024^3.

The parsed value is stored in \fIdest\fR.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes successfully consumed from the source string.
If no suffix is found, it acts like \fBscan_ulonglong\fR.